'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... isp_hub75_morphTime.spin2
''   Purpose.... Shared time base for the morphing digits: wrap-safe elapsed milliseconds, a frame-rate meter and the motion constants
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 12 Oct 2026
''   Version.... v1.0.0
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ One clock for the whole program. Its state is in DAT, so every object that includes this file
  (the frame loop, a group, a test) reads and writes the same total: there is one time base, not
  one per group. Keep this object free of CON overrides: an override that changed its image
  would give that instance its own DAT and split the clock (p2kb p2kbSpin2ObjectImageDedup).

  Usage (one cog, the one that runs the frame loop; R-1.5, no cogs of our own):
    1. reset()                  - once, before the frame loop starts (update() calls it on first use)
    2. nowMs := update()        - once per frame, before anything is drawn: reads the counter once,
                                  adds the time since the last call, counts the frame
    3. pass nowMs down          - every group, digit and segment animates from this one value
    4. framesPerSecondX100()    - the meter's figure for a live FPS group or a performance test

  Wrap: getct() is the low 32 bits of the system counter and wraps every 2^32 ticks (12.82 s at
  335 MHz). Time is added up from getct() differences, which are exact modulo 2^32, and divided
  unsigned, so any gap shorter than one wrap is counted in full. update() must therefore run at
  least once per wrap period; a frame loop runs it every refresh (about 14 ms on the quad). A gap
  longer than one wrap loses whole wraps (12.82 s each at 335 MHz) and cannot be detected here.

  Units: milliseconds as a LONG. The total passes 2^31 after 24.8 days and 2^32 after 49.7 days;
  compare two times by subtracting them (later - earlier), never with < or >, and the difference
  stays right for any span under 24.8 days.
}

CON ' time base units

  MS_PER_SECOND = 1000                                          ' converts clkfreq (ticks per second) to ticks per millisecond
  FPS_SCALE = 100                                               ' the frame rate is reported times this (two decimals)
  FPS_WINDOW_MS = 1000                                          ' the meter publishes a new figure once per window of at least this length

CON ' motion settings shared by every level (group, digit, segment)

  DEFAULT_MOVE_MS = 300                                         ' a move's duration when the caller sets none (spec R-5.4's example)

  ' how a move's position follows its time (morphCounters.setEasing()):
  '   EASE_LINEAR - constant speed: the position is the fraction of the duration that has passed (the 2021 look)
  '   EASE_SMOOTH - smoothstep, 3p^2 - 2p^3: starts and ends slowly, with no jump in speed at either end
  #0, EASE_LINEAR, EASE_SMOOTH

  ' how a moving segment's lit part ends (morphCounters.setProfile(); spec R-5.3):
  '   PROFILE_EDGE - solid, then one fractional edge pixel (plan profile A)
  '   PROFILE_TAIL - solid, then a gradient tail several pixels long (plan profile C)
  #0, PROFILE_EDGE, PROFILE_TAIL
  DEFAULT_PROFILE = PROFILE_TAIL
  TAIL_DIVISOR = 4                                              ' PROFILE_TAIL's tail when the caller sets none: a quarter of the segment's length
  MIN_TAIL_PIXELS = 1                                           ' the shortest tail: one pixel (PROFILE_EDGE's edge)

DAT ' shared clock (one copy for the program; see the notes above)

  prevTick        long    0                                     ' the counter at the last update()
  leftoverTicks   long    0                                     ' ticks below one millisecond, carried to the next update()
  msTotal         long    0                                     ' milliseconds since reset()
  ticksPerMs      long    0                                     ' clkfreq / MS_PER_SECOND; 0 means reset() has not run
  windowStartMs   long    0                                     ' msTotal when the current meter window began
  windowFrames    long    0                                     ' update() calls in the current meter window
  fpsLatestX100   long    0                                     ' frames per second x FPS_SCALE over the last completed window

PUB null()
'' This is NOT a top level object.
''

PUB reset()
'' Start the time base at zero and clear the frame-rate meter.
''

    ticksPerMs := clkfreq / MS_PER_SECOND
    prevTick := getct()
    leftoverTicks := 0
    msTotal := 0
    windowStartMs := 0
    windowFrames := 0
    fpsLatestX100 := 0


PUB update() : nowMs | nowTick, deltaTicks, carryTicks, windowMs
'' Read the system counter once, add the time since the last call, count one frame and return the total.
''
'' @returns nowMs - Milliseconds since reset(); compare times by subtracting them

' Local Variables:
' @local nowTick - The system counter now
' @local deltaTicks - Ticks since the last call, modulo 2^32: exact for any gap shorter than one counter wrap
' @local carryTicks - Ticks below one millisecond, this call's and the ones carried from earlier calls
' @local windowMs - Length of the current meter window so far

    if ticksPerMs == 0
        reset()                                                 ' first use without reset(): the time base starts now
    nowTick := getct()
    deltaTicks := nowTick - prevTick
    prevTick := nowTick
    ' unsigned divide and remainder: a gap of 2^31 ticks or more (6.41 s at 335 MHz) is still positive
    msTotal += deltaTicks +/ ticksPerMs
    carryTicks := (deltaTicks +// ticksPerMs) + leftoverTicks
    if carryTicks +>= ticksPerMs
        msTotal++
        carryTicks -= ticksPerMs
    leftoverTicks := carryTicks
    nowMs := msTotal

    ' frame-rate meter: a counter and a compare per frame; the division runs once per window
    windowFrames++
    windowMs := msTotal - windowStartMs
    if windowMs >= FPS_WINDOW_MS
        fpsLatestX100 := muldiv64(windowFrames, FPS_SCALE * MS_PER_SECOND, windowMs)
        windowStartMs := msTotal
        windowFrames := 0


PUB elapsedMs() : nowMs
'' Return the total as of the last update(), without reading the counter (the current frame's time).
''
'' @returns nowMs - Milliseconds since reset(); compare times by subtracting them

    nowMs := msTotal


PUB framesPerSecondX100() : rateX100
'' Return the frame rate over the last completed meter window, times FPS_SCALE (7107 means 71.07 frames per second).
''
'' @returns rateX100 - Frames per second x FPS_SCALE; 0 until the first window of FPS_WINDOW_MS completes

    rateX100 := fpsLatestX100


CON ' license

